    "warnings": [
      "sh001: locked frame with a travelling set. The whitebox rig translates downward with Alice at her 0.088 m/s drift so she holds frame position exactly as camera.json describes; there is no pan, tilt, reframe or lens change.",
      "SCN-falling-dream is modelled as ONE 6 m repeating rig section with a single static instance of each fitting (cupboards y 0.4-2.6, bookshelves y 1.2-3.6, pantry shelf y 4.9-5.2, map pegs y 3.5-4.5, picture pegs y 4.15-4.65). The 48 s descent is carried in the plate by the dressing travelling upward; the whitebox cannot show that, so Alice's modelled altitude is a monotonic drift through the section and does NOT line up with the fitting named in each shot."
    ],
    "authored": true,
    "issues": [
      {
        "issue_id": "WBI-ep01-grp001-001",
        "kind": "model_gap",
        "severity": "blocking",
        "plan_status": "open",
        "question": "SCN-falling-dream is modelled at the Bible's 2.4 m brick shaft with a 1.7 m clear fall column. The lateral wides cannot be framed in it: sh001/sh022 (28 mm, Alice at 0.20 of frame height) need 7.88 m of standoff and sh021 needs 3.13 m, but the widest in-model camera is about 1.5 m, so the reference shows a near-full-figure frame where the shot is a wide. Ship that, or re-model the shaft?",
        "provisional": "Hold the authored view axis, lens and camera height, place the lens at the largest standoff inside the modelled clear column (Alice biased 0.35 m down-axis, standoff 1.50 m), and accept a whitebox frame that is tighter than composition's size_in_frame. Axis, eyeline, relative geometry and the descent rate stay correct; only the field of view is wrong.",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "remodel",
            "label": "Re-model SCN-falling-dream at the dream shaft diameter the wides imply (about 16 m across for sh001/sh022)",
            "consequence": "p4-scene-model re-issues bible/scenes/SCN-falling-dream/whitebox.json and the layout; grp001/grp008/grp009/grp010 are re-staged and the whitebox then matches the storyboard wides. Costs one scene-model pass before H3W can be signed.",
            "cost": "one scene-model re-issue + re-stage of 4 groups",
            "rewrites": [
              "bible/scenes/SCN-falling-dream/whitebox.json",
              "assets/concepts/scenes/SCN-falling-dream/layout.json"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "tight",
            "label": "Ship the whitebox at the tighter in-model frame (the default) and let the shot prompt carry the wide",
            "consequence": "No re-model. The camera reference video for sh001, sh017-sh025 shows a tighter frame than the shot; 08-video-gen must read the size code from the prompt, not from the whitebox video.",
            "cost": "none"
          },
